n-Hodgkin's lymphomas</article-title><source>Hematol Oncol</source><year>2005</year><volume>23</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>10</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/hon.743</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Tsang RW, Gospodarowicz MK (2005) Radiation therapy for localized low-grade non-Hodgkin's lymphomas. Hematol Oncol 23(1):10&#x02013;17 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16158458</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karam</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Novak</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Cyriac</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ali</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Nazeer</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Nugent</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of fluorine-18 fluoro-deoxyglucose positron emission tomography scan in the evaluation and follow-up of patients with low-grade lymphomas</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>2006</year><volume>107</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>175</fpage><lpage>183</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/cncr.21967</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Karam M, Novak L, Cyriac J, Ali A, Nazeer T, Nugent F (2006) Role of fluorine-18 fluoro-deoxyglucose positron emission tomography scan in the evaluation and follow-up of patients with low-grade lymphomas. Cancer 107(1):175&#x02013;183 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16721817</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jerusalem</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Beguin</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Najjar</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Positron emission tomography (PET) with 18F-fluorodeoxyglucose (18F-FDG) for the staging of low-grade non-Hodgkin&#x02019;s lymphoma (NHL)</article-title><source>Ann Oncol</source><year>2001</year><volume>12</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>825</fpage><lpage>830</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1023/A:1011169332265</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Jerusalem G, Beguin Y, Najjar F et al (2001) Positron emission tomography (PET) with 18F-fluorodeoxyglucose (18F-FDG) for the staging of low-grade non-Hodgkin&#x02019;s lymphoma (NHL). Ann Oncol 12(6):825&#x02013;830 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11484959</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jerusalem</surname><given-names>GH</given-names></name><name><surname>Beguin</surname><given-names>YP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Positron emission tomography in non-Hodgkin&#x02019;s lymphoma (NHL): relationship between tracer uptake and pathological findings, including preliminary experience in the staging of low-grade NHL</article-title><source>Clin Lymphoma</source><year>2002</year><volume>3</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>56</fpage><lpage>61</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3816/CLM.2002.n.012</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Jerusalem GH, Beguin YP (2002) Positron emission tomography in non-Hodgkin&#x02019;s lymphoma (NHL): relationship between tracer uptake and pathological findings, including preliminary experience in the staging of low-grade NHL. Clin Lymphoma 3(1):56&#x02013;61 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12141957</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blum</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Seymour</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Wirth</surname><given-names>A</gi